{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 8, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the quaternions: dimension 4 over the reals, basis 1, i, j, k\n  commutative: no: i j = k but j i = -k\n  associative: yes ((ab)c = a(bc) at 200 random triples); by Frobenius, R, C and H are the only associative real division algebras\n  alternative: yes ((aa)b = a(ab), (ba)a = b(aa) at 200 random pairs)\n  flexible and power-associative: yes ((ab)a = a(ba); powers a^n are well defined), as in every Cayley-Dickson algebra\n  normed (a composition algebra): yes, |ab| = |a||b| at 200 random pairs (Euler's four-square identity)\n  a division algebra: yes, ab = 0 only when a = 0 or b = 0 (it is normed); by Hurwitz, R, C, H and O are the only normed division algebras\n  inverses: every a != 0 has a^-1 = conj(a)/|a|^2 (a a^-1 = 1, checked)\n  conjugation: conj(ab) = conj(b) conj(a) (checked); a conj(a) = |a|^2\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 8, "ok": true, "cmd": "algebra", "ucas": "algebra quaternion", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "algebra", "commutative": "no: i j = k but j i = -k", "associative": "yes ((ab)c = a(bc) at 200 random triples); by Frobenius, R, C and H are the only associative real division algebras", "alternative": "yes ((aa)b = a(ab), (ba)a = b(aa) at 200 random pairs)", "flexible_and_power_associative": "yes ((ab)a = a(ba); powers a^n are well defined), as in every Cayley-Dickson algebra", "normed_a_composition_algebra": "yes, |ab| = |a||b| at 200 random pairs (Euler's four-square identity)", "a_division_algebra": "yes, ab = 0 only when a = 0 or b = 0 (it is normed); by Hurwitz, R, C, H and O are the only normed division algebras", "inverses": "every a != 0 has a^-1 = conj(a)/|a|^2 (a a^-1 = 1, checked)", "conjugation": "conj(ab) = conj(b) conj(a) (checked); a conj(a) = |a|^2", "headline": "the quaternions: dimension 4 over the reals, basis 1, i, j, k"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "the quaternions: dimension 4 over the reals, basis 1, i, j, k\n  commutative: no: i j = k but j i = -k\n  associative: yes ((ab)c = a(bc) at 200 random triples); by Frobenius, R, C and H are the only associative real division algebras\n  alternative: yes ((aa)b = a(ab), (ba)a = b(aa) at 200 random pairs)\n  flexible and power-associative: yes ((ab)a = a(ba); powers a^n are well defined), as in every Cayley-Dickson algebra\n  normed (a composition algebra): yes, |ab| = |a||b| at 200 random pairs (Euler's four-square identity)\n  a division algebra: yes, ab = 0 only when a = 0 or b = 0 (it is normed); by Hurwitz, R, C, H and O are the only normed division algebras\n  inverses: every a != 0 has a^-1 = conj(a)/|a|^2 (a a^-1 = 1, checked)\n  conjugation: conj(ab) = conj(b) conj(a) (checked); a conj(a) = |a|^2\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 9, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the octonions: dimension 8 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7\n  commutative: no: e1 e2 = e3 but e2 e1 = -e3\n  associative: no: (e1 e2) e4 = e7 but e1 (e2 e4) = -e7\n  alternative: yes ((aa)b = a(ab), (ba)a = b(aa) at 200 random pairs); by Artin's theorem any two elements generate an associative subalgebra\n  flexible and power-associative: yes ((ab)a = a(ba); powers a^n are well defined), as in every Cayley-Dickson algebra\n  normed (a composition algebra): yes, |ab| = |a||b| at 200 random pairs (Degen's eight-square identity)\n  a division algebra: yes, ab = 0 only when a = 0 or b = 0 (it is normed); by Hurwitz, R, C, H and O are the only normed division algebras\n  inverses: every a != 0 has a^-1 = conj(a)/|a|^2 (a a^-1 = 1, checked); a^-1(ab) = b holds (alternativity)\n  conjugation: conj(ab) = conj(b) conj(a) (checked); a conj(a) = |a|^2\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 9, "ok": true, "cmd": "algebra", "ucas": "algebra octonion", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "algebra", "commutative": "no: e1 e2 = e3 but e2 e1 = -e3", "associative": "no: (e1 e2) e4 = e7 but e1 (e2 e4) = -e7", "alternative": "yes ((aa)b = a(ab), (ba)a = b(aa) at 200 random pairs); by Artin's theorem any two elements generate an associative subalgebra", "flexible_and_power_associative": "yes ((ab)a = a(ba); powers a^n are well defined), as in every Cayley-Dickson algebra", "normed_a_composition_algebra": "yes, |ab| = |a||b| at 200 random pairs (Degen's eight-square identity)", "a_division_algebra": "yes, ab = 0 only when a = 0 or b = 0 (it is normed); by Hurwitz, R, C, H and O are the only normed division algebras", "inverses": "every a != 0 has a^-1 = conj(a)/|a|^2 (a a^-1 = 1, checked); a^-1(ab) = b holds (alternativity)", "conjugation": "conj(ab) = conj(b) conj(a) (checked); a conj(a) = |a|^2", "headline": "the octonions: dimension 8 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "the octonions: dimension 8 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7\n  commutative: no: e1 e2 = e3 but e2 e1 = -e3\n  associative: no: (e1 e2) e4 = e7 but e1 (e2 e4) = -e7\n  alternative: yes ((aa)b = a(ab), (ba)a = b(aa) at 200 random pairs); by Artin's theorem any two elements generate an associative subalgebra\n  flexible and power-associative: yes ((ab)a = a(ba); powers a^n are well defined), as in every Cayley-Dickson algebra\n  normed (a composition algebra): yes, |ab| = |a||b| at 200 random pairs (Degen's eight-square identity)\n  a division algebra: yes, ab = 0 only when a = 0 or b = 0 (it is normed); by Hurwitz, R, C, H and O are the only normed division algebras\n  inverses: every a != 0 has a^-1 = conj(a)/|a|^2 (a a^-1 = 1, checked); a^-1(ab) = b holds (alternativity)\n  conjugation: conj(ab) = conj(b) conj(a) (checked); a conj(a) = |a|^2\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 10, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "multiplication table of the quaternions (row times column), not symmetric: the product does not commute:\n      |   1   i   j   k\n  ----+----------------\n    1 |   1   i   j   k\n    i |   i  -1   k  -j\n    j |   j  -k  -1   i\n    k |   k   j  -i  -1\n  i^2 = j^2 = k^2 = ijk = -1 (Hamilton); ij = k, jk = i, ki = j, and reversing a product changes its sign\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 10, "ok": true, "cmd": "multiplication_table", "ucas": "table quaternion", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "multiplication_table", "headline": "multiplication table of the quaternions (row times column), not symmetric: the product does not commute:", "details": ["|   1   i   j   k", "----+----------------", "1 |   1   i   j   k", "i |   i  -1   k  -j", "j |   j  -k  -1   i", "k |   k   j  -i  -1", "i^2 = j^2 = k^2 = ijk = -1 (Hamilton); ij = k, jk = i, ki = j, and reversing a product changes its sign"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "multiplication table of the quaternions (row times column), not symmetric: the product does not commute:\n      |   1   i   j   k\n  ----+----------------\n    1 |   1   i   j   k\n    i |   i  -1   k  -j\n    j |   j  -k  -1   i\n    k |   k   j  -i  -1\n  i^2 = j^2 = k^2 = ijk = -1 (Hamilton); ij = k, jk = i, ki = j, and reversing a product changes its sign\n"}, "isError": false}}
